---
// Rung 2 of the SIP ladder. The spine (dd-005).
//
// The planner's two-rates rung asks what the pot really grows at against what
// is really being taken out. The accumulation twin asks what the money really
// grows at against what a contribution is really worth - because the saver's
// two forces are the same two forces, pointing the other way.
//
// It discharges dd-004 for this page. "Your money grows 13.4%, prices rise 6%,
// so you are really 7% better off" teaches the real/nominal distinction in the
// reader's own words without ever using either word, and it has to be taught
// here, because every screen after this one depends on it.
//
// The falling-contribution row is the one thing most SIP calculators never say:
// a fixed monthly amount is a smaller sacrifice and a smaller contribution
// every year. The step-up control in the last rung is the answer to it, and
// this is where the reader learns why it exists.
---

<section id="rungSipRates" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-4" aria-labelledby="rungSipRatesQ">
  <div class="card-premium rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6">

    <div>
      <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.11em] text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">
        Next question
      </p>
      <h2 id="rungSipRatesQ" class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 mt-1">
        So how fast is your money really growing?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400 mt-2">
        Everything below turns on this one comparison.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The ledger. Deliberately plain: one thing going up, one thing pulling
         it down, and the gap between them. -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-700 divide-y divide-navy-200 dark:divide-navy-700 overflow-hidden">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3">
        <span class="text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">Your savings grow by</span>
        <span id="sipRateGross" class="text-base font-semibold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">—</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3">
        <span class="text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
          The fund takes
          <span class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">whatever the market does</span>
        </span>
        <span id="sipRateFee" class="text-base font-semibold tabular-nums text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400">—</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3">
        <span class="text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
          Prices rise by
          <span class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">so the same rupee buys less each year</span>
        </span>
        <span id="sipRateInflation" class="text-base font-semibold tabular-nums text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400">—</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3 bg-navy-50/60 dark:bg-navy-900/40">
        <span class="text-sm font-medium text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200">
          So you are genuinely better off by
          <span class="block text-xs font-normal text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">these compound, they do not subtract</span>
        </span>
        <span id="sipRateReal" class="text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">—</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3">
        <span class="text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
          And you are putting in
          <span class="block text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">every month, for the whole term</span>
        </span>
        <span id="sipRateContribution" class="text-base font-semibold tabular-nums text-gold-700 dark:text-gold-400">—</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3.5 bg-navy-50/60 dark:bg-navy-900/40">
        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">
          Which by the last year is really worth
          <span class="block text-xs font-normal text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">the same amount, in today's money</span>
        </span>
        <span id="sipRateLastReal" class="text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">—</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      <p id="sipRatesInsight" class="text-base leading-relaxed text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200"></p>
      <p id="sipRatesIdea" class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="pt-4 border-t border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
      <p id="sipRatesHandoff" class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400"></p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import {
    contributionPlan, instalmentInYear, realRateChain,
  } from '../../utils/sipAdvice';

  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id);
  const pct = (n: number, dp = 1) => `${n >= 0 ? '' : '−'}${Math.abs(n).toFixed(dp)}%`;
  const grp = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-IN');

  function render(detail: any) {
    const { inputs } = detail;
    const g = inputs.expectedReturn;
    const i = inputs.expectedInflation;
    const years = inputs.horizonYears;

    // ONE definition of the chain, shared with rung 4 (sol-038). This used to
    // be a second hand-written copy of the same ratio, and when the fund fee was
    // added to rung 4's copy and not to this one the page printed 6.7% and 6.9%
    // for the identical quantity.
    const chain = realRateChain(inputs);
    const real = chain.real;

    // What the LAST instalment is worth in today's money. A step-up pushes the
    // nominal figure up; inflation pulls the real one down; this row is where
    // the two meet, and it is the argument for the step-up control.
    // dd-017 / sol-035. This read `inputs.annualStepUp`, a field that no longer
    // exists - the contribution's escalation is derived from the mode now - so
    // it produced NaN and printed it. The rung asks the engine's own derivation
    // rather than re-deriving the schedule from a field it hopes is there.
    const plan = contributionPlan(inputs);
    const lastNominal = instalmentInYear(inputs, years);
    const lastReal = lastNominal / Math.pow(1 + i / 100, years - 1);

    $('sipRateGross')!.textContent = `+ ${pct(chain.growth)} a year`;
    $('sipRateFee')!.textContent = `− ${pct(chain.fee, 2)} a year`;
    $('sipRateInflation')!.textContent = `− ${pct(chain.inflation)} a year`;
    $('sipRateReal')!.textContent = `${pct(real, 1)} a year`;
    $('sipRateContribution')!.textContent = `₹${grp(plan.monthly)} a month`;
    $('sipRateLastReal')!.textContent = `₹${grp(lastReal)} a month`;

    const gap = plan.monthly > 0 ? lastReal / plan.monthly : 0;
    const lastRow = $('sipRateLastReal') as HTMLElement;
    lastRow.className =
      'text-lg font-bold tabular-nums ' +
      (gap >= 0.98
        ? 'text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400'
        : gap >= 0.7
          ? 'text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400'
          : 'text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400');

    // The rung's argument changed with dd-017 and the copy had to change with
    // it. It used to be "a fixed instalment shrinks, so consider a step-up".
    // Holding purchasing power is the DEFAULT now, so the interesting sentence
    // is what that costs in cash - and the shrinking version is only true for
    // someone who has deliberately chosen a flat rupee amount.
    if (real <= 0) {
      $('sipRatesInsight')!.textContent =
        `Your savings grow ${pct(g)} while prices rise ${pct(i)}, so in what the ` +
        `money can actually buy you are going backwards. Every year of this plan ` +
        `costs you real money, however healthy the balance looks on the statement.`;
    } else if (!plan.holdsPurchasingPower) {
      $('sipRatesInsight')!.textContent =
        `Your savings grow ${pct(g)}, but prices rise ${pct(i)}, so you are only ` +
        `genuinely ${pct(real, 1)} better off each year. And you have chosen to ` +
        `keep the instalment at ₹${grp(plan.monthly)} while everything around it ` +
        `gets dearer — by year ${years} it is really worth ₹${grp(lastReal)} a ` +
        `month, about ${Math.round(gap * 100)}% of what it costs you today. That ` +
        `is a decision to save less every year, not a neutral one.`;
    } else if (plan.realStep > 0) {
      $('sipRatesInsight')!.textContent =
        `Your savings grow ${pct(g)}, but prices rise ${pct(i)}, so you are ` +
        `genuinely ${pct(real, 1)} better off each year. Your instalment keeps ` +
        `pace with prices and adds ${pct(plan.realStep * 100)} a year on top, so ` +
        `by year ${years} you are paying ₹${grp(lastNominal)} a month — worth ` +
        `₹${grp(lastReal)} in today's money, more than the ₹${grp(plan.monthly)} ` +
        `you start with. You are saving harder in real terms every year.`;
    } else {
      $('sipRatesInsight')!.textContent =
        `Your savings grow ${pct(g)}, but prices rise ${pct(i)}, so you are ` +
        `genuinely ${pct(real, 1)} better off each year. The same erosion applies ` +
        `to what you put in, which is why your instalment rises with prices: by ` +
        `year ${years} you are paying ₹${grp(lastNominal)} a month, and that is ` +
        `still the same ₹${grp(plan.monthly)} of spending power you are giving ` +
        `up today. What it costs you never changes.`;
    }

    $('sipRatesIdea')!.textContent =
      `This is the comparison worth carrying away. Not the final balance, not ` +
      `the odds — just these two rates and what they do to a fixed monthly ` +
      `amount. Anything that helps pushes the first one up or the second one ` +
      `down, and anything that hurts does the reverse.`;

    $('sipRatesHandoff')!.innerHTML =
      `And there are three things that eat into that ` +
      `<span class="font-medium text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200">${pct(real, 1)}</span> ` +
      `before you ever see it: <span class="font-medium text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200">tax when you sell</span>, ` +
      `<span class="font-medium text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200">a market that is rougher than the average suggests</span>, and ` +
      `<span class="font-medium text-navy-800 dark:text-navy-200">anything you pay to protect yourself</span>. ` +
      `Each gets its own step.`;
  }

  window.addEventListener('sip:result', (e) => render((e as CustomEvent).detail));
</script>
